sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Typed IPC round trip for the registry snapshot
    accDescr: On shell boot the React frontend invokes the registry_snapshot command through the Tauri IPC bridge. The Rust command returns the built-in registry snapshot DTO, which was generated into TypeScript bindings at build time. If no runtime is detected the bridge reports an honest error instead of fabricating data.
    participant UI as React shell
    participant BR as invokeIpc bridge
    participant RS as Tauri runtime
    participant CMD as registry_snapshot command
    participant REG as zettings-core seed graph

    UI->>BR: invokeIpc("registry_snapshot")
    alt inside desktop runtime
        BR->>RS: invoke(command)
        RS->>CMD: call
        CMD->>REG: built_in_categories()
        REG-->>CMD: CategorySummary map
        CMD-->>RS: RegistrySnapshotDto
        RS-->>BR: JSON payload (bindings-typed)
        BR-->>UI: RegistrySnapshotDto
    else plain browser dev session
        BR-->>UI: Error "Zettings runtime not detected"
    end
